COMMON TRAPS

- ⚠️ Confusing Allylic vs Vinylic: Allylic is sp³ C next to C=C; Vinylic is X directly on C=C.
- ⚠️ Chlorobenzene is NOT benzylic: Benzylic needs an sp³ carbon bridge.
- ⚠️ HX vs PX₃: HX forms carbocations (Rearrange!); PX₃ is SN2 (Invert, NO rearrange).
- ⚠️ Peroxide Rule: ONLY for HBr. HCl/HI follow Markovnikov even with peroxide.
- ⚠️ Silver Salt + I₂: It's NOT R-I, it is an ESTER.
- ⚠️ Meta NO₂ in NSR: Does NOT stabilize the carbanion; rate boost is negligible compared to O/P.
- ⚠️ Bridgehead halides: Inert to SN1, SN2, and Elimination (cannot be planar/back-side attack blocked).
- ⚠️ SN1 Racemization: Never 100% racemic; inversion slightly predominates.

